CONTEXT FROM TEXTBOOK:
This figure is a four-column chart showing how different plane cuts through a double cone produce different curves, with cone drawings across the top row and the resulting curves below. Each cone is drawn identically in pale blue as two nappes meeting point to point, the upper rim a solid blue ellipse and the lower rim a dashed one, and a red curve marks where a cutting plane meets it. The columns are titled Diagonal Slice, Horizontal Slice, Deep Vertical Slice, and Vertical Slice. The first shows a red ellipse tilted across the upper nappe; the second a red ellipse lying level across the upper nappe; the third two red arcs, one curving up through the top nappe and one down through the bottom; the fourth a single red arc cutting downward through the lower nappe only. Below each cone the curve is named and redrawn on its own in red, free of the cone: Ellipse as a flattened oval, Circle as a round closed curve, Hyperbola as two opposing branches, Parabola as a single upward-opening arc. Keeping each slice above its isolated curve lets the angle of the cut be read directly against the shape it yields. The chart sorts the four nondegenerate conic sections by the orientation of the generating plane.

PROJECTION TYPE: axonometric
Use ordinary orthographic projection: setCameraView({ projection: 'orthographic', axisScreenAngles, heightFraction }). If the plan gives axis_screen_angles: null (a flat 2D plot/diagram), pass axisScreenAngles: null for a front-on view. Otherwise the plan does not measure per-figure angles — use a standard isometric pose: axisScreenAngles: { x: 30, z: 30 }. The source image is a PROJECTION of a 3D object: rebuild the true object — a rectangle stays a rectangle in world space — and let the camera do the projecting. Never bake the drawn parallelogram into the geometry, and never shear geometry. Omit zoom and call setCameraView after all geometry is added — the scaffold auto-fits from the projected bounding box.

ELEMENTS TO RECREATE IN 3D:
  - double cone: two right-circular nappes meeting apex-to-apex at the origin, axis vertical
  - pale blue translucent cone surface (both nappes)
  - dark blue outline slant edges on left and right silhouette of each nappe
  - solid blue ellipse rim at the top of the upper nappe
  - dashed blue ellipse rim at the bottom of the lower nappe (hidden far half of the base)
  - red intersection curve where the cutting plane meets the cone (closed ellipse/circle, single parabolic arc, or two hyperbolic branches)
  - semi-transparent cutting plane (light gray quad) that tilts through the cone
  - small red directional arrowheads on the intersection arcs for the vertical/deep-vertical cases, matching the source
  - column title text above the cone: 'Diagonal Slice' / 'Horizontal Slice' / 'Deep Vertical Slice' / 'Vertical Slice'
  - curve name text below: 'Ellipse' / 'Circle' / 'Hyperbola' / 'Parabola'
  - isolated flat red curve redrawn alone, free of the cone (flattened oval, circle, two opposing branches, single upward-opening arc)

GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
Double cone: apex at the world origin, axis along +Y. Each nappe has base radius 1.4 and height 2.0, so the half-angle from the axis is 35° measured as atan(1.4/2.0) — for clean math treat the cone as slope 1 (radius = |y| scaled so the slant sits at 45° from horizontal); total figure spans y ∈ [-2, 2], x,z ∈ [-1.4, 1.4]. Upper rim at y = +2 is a SOLID dark-blue circle drawn as an ellipse in the projected view (vertical squash ~0.32); lower rim at y = -2 is the same circle with its far half DASHED and near half solid, exactly as in the source. Silhouette slant edges drawn as dark-blue lines from apex to each rim. Palette: cone fill pale blue #ccd9f0 at ~0.55 opacity, cone outlines and rims #1f3a6b / #2b4f9e, all intersection and isolated curves red #d9453d at ~2.5px, title and label text near-black #1a1a1a bold sans-serif. Cutting plane: a 4×4 light-gray translucent quad (#9aa4b0, opacity 0.25) passing through the point (0, +0.9, 0) for the elliptical/circular cases and offset horizontally to x = -0.5 for the steep cases so it misses the apex; it pivots about the world Z axis by the slider angle θ from horizontal. Classification with cone slant 45°: θ = 0 circle; 0 < θ < 45 ellipse (tilted oval on the UPPER nappe only, matching the first column); θ = 45 parabola (single arc opening upward, cutting the LOWER nappe as in the fourth column, with two small red arrowheads at its open ends); θ > 45 hyperbola (two branches, upper branch curving up inside the top nappe and lower branch curving down inside the bottom nappe, arrowheads on all four open ends as in the third column). In 'Curve alone' mode, hide the cone and plane and present the red curve face-on in its own plane, centered, scaled to ~2.2 units wide, with the name label below: Ellipse = flattened oval (semi-axes 1.1 × 0.35), Circle = radius 0.8, Hyperbola = two branches opening away from each other vertically with vertices at y = ±0.35, Parabola = single upward-opening arc, vertex at the bottom center.

DISCRETE CONTROLS (implement every one of these in #ui, each must work independently):
[
  {
    "id": "planeTilt",
    "type": "slider",
    "label": "Cutting-plane tilt from horizontal (°)",
    "range": [
      0,
      80,
      1
    ],
    "default": 25,
    "teaches": "The conic type is set purely by how the plane's tilt compares with the cone's 45° slant: level gives a circle, shallower than the slant gives an ellipse, exactly at the slant gives a parabola, steeper gives the two branches of a hyperbola."
  },
  {
    "id": "viewMode",
    "type": "toggle",
    "label": "View",
    "options": [
      "Cone slice",
      "Curve alone"
    ],
    "default": "Cone slice",
    "teaches": "The red curve drawn on the cone and the named planar graph below are the same object — the intersection flattened into its own plane."
  },
  {
    "id": "conicStep",
    "type": "state",
    "label": "Conic section",
    "states": [
      "Ellipse (diagonal slice)",
      "Circle (horizontal slice)",
      "Hyperbola (deep vertical slice)",
      "Parabola (vertical slice)"
    ],
    "default": "Ellipse (diagonal slice)",
    "teaches": "The four nondegenerate conics form one ordered family, classified by the direction of the generating plane."
  },
  {
    "id": "orbitCone",
    "type": "orbit",
    "teaches": "Seeing the cut from other angles shows the red curve is a genuine 3D curve lying in a flat plane, not a shape drawn on the cone's surface."
  }
]

DEMO STEPS (tween through these using goToStep(); each step drives the controls above):
[
  {
    "title": "Diagonal Slice → Ellipse",
    "narration": "A plane tilted about 25° cuts clean through the upper nappe, and the closed red curve is a stretched oval: an ellipse.",
    "state": {
      "conicStep": "Ellipse (diagonal slice)",
      "planeTilt": 25,
      "viewMode": "Cone slice"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Flatten it",
    "narration": "Lift the ellipse out of the cone and view it face-on — the same red curve is the planar graph labeled Ellipse.",
    "state": {
      "conicStep": "Ellipse (diagonal slice)",
      "planeTilt": 25,
      "viewMode": "Curve alone"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Horizontal Slice → Circle",
    "narration": "Level the plane to 0°. The cut is perpendicular to the axis and the ellipse closes up into a perfect circle.",
    "state": {
      "conicStep": "Circle (horizontal slice)",
      "planeTilt": 0,
      "viewMode": "Cone slice"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Vertical Slice → Parabola",
    "narration": "Tilt the plane until it is exactly parallel to the cone's slant edge (45°). The curve can no longer close: it runs off to infinity as a single parabolic arc through the lower nappe.",
    "state": {
      "conicStep": "Parabola (vertical slice)",
      "planeTilt": 45,
      "viewMode": "Cone slice"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Deep Vertical Slice → Hyperbola",
    "narration": "Past 45° the plane is steep enough to reach both nappes at once, so the intersection splits into two opposing red branches — a hyperbola.",
    "state": {
      "conicStep": "Hyperbola (deep vertical slice)",
      "planeTilt": 70,
      "viewMode": "Cone slice"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Compare the four graphs",
    "narration": "Switch to the isolated curves and step back through the sequence: oval, circle, two branches, single arc — the full set of nondegenerate conic sections.",
    "state": {
      "conicStep": "Hyperbola (deep vertical slice)",
      "planeTilt": 70,
      "viewMode": "Curve alone"
    }
  }
]

CAMERA VIEW (framing only). Call setCameraView({ projection, ...these }) AFTER all geometry is added. Keep the projection MECHANISM from PROJECTION TYPE above (orthographic / sheared-oblique / perspective). For perspective these params set the pose (azimuth/elevation/roll); for the two parallel projections pose is a standard default (see PROJECTION TYPE above), and these params set only roll and framing (heightFraction):
{
  "rollDeg": 0,
  "heightFraction": 0.7
}

NOTES: Build the cone from two THREE.ConeGeometry instances (openEnded, one flipped) with MeshBasicMaterial, side: DoubleSide, transparent, depthWrite false so the red curve reads through the surface. Draw rims and slant edges as Line2/LineSegments; use a LineDashedMaterial (computeLineDistances) for the hidden far half of the bottom rim. Compute the intersection curve analytically rather than by mesh boolean: parameterize the plane, substitute into y^2 = k(x^2+z^2) and sample 200 points per branch, rebuilding the BufferGeometry each slider frame; clamp sampling to the cone's y ∈ [-2, 2] so branches terminate at the rims. Arrowheads as small ConeGeometry cones oriented along the curve tangent at the terminal samples. Labels as CSS2DObject / sprite text so they stay upright during orbit. Cross-fade (300 ms) between 'Cone slice' and 'Curve alone' by fading cone+plane opacity to 0 while lerping the camera to a face-on view of the cutting plane, then flattening the curve into the screen plane. The state button snaps planeTilt to 25 / 0 / 70 / 45 respectively and flashes the matching title and curve-name labels in red.

Follow the interaction plan above.

Here is the generated code to evaluate:

<!-- @FIGURE_UI_BEGIN -->
<div style="font-weight:700;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:2px">Conic sections from a double cone</div>

<div style="font-weight:600;margin-top:2px">Conic section</div>
<button id="btnKEllipse" class="kbtn">Ellipse (diagonal slice)</button>
<button id="btnKCircle" class="kbtn">Circle (horizontal slice)</button>
<button id="btnKHyper" class="kbtn">Hyperbola (deep vertical slice)</button>
<button id="btnKPara" class="kbtn">Parabola (vertical slice)</button>

<label style="margin-top:6px">Cutting-plane tilt from horizontal: <b id="tiltVal">25&deg;</b>
  <input type="range" id="planeTilt" min="0" max="80" step="1" value="25">
</label>
<div id="classNote" style="font-size:10px;color:#555;line-height:1.35">cone slant = 45&deg;; tilt &lt; 45&deg; &rarr; ellipse, = 45&deg; &rarr; parabola, &gt; 45&deg; &rarr; hyperbola</div>

<div style="font-weight:600;margin-top:4px">View</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:4px">
  <button id="btnViewCone">Cone slice</button>
  <button id="btnViewFlat">Curve alone</button>
</div>
<label style="flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-top:2px">
  <input type="checkbox" id="chkPlane" checked> Show cutting plane
</label>

<div style="font-weight:600;margin-top:4px">Guided demo</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:4px">
  <button id="btnPrev">&#9664; Prev</button>
  <button id="btnPlay">&#9654; Play</button>
  <button id="btnNext">Next &#9654;</button>
</div>
<div id="stepTitle" style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;margin-top:2px"></div>
<div id="narration" style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.4;color:#333"></div>

<div style="font-size:10px;color:#666;margin-top:4px">Drag to orbit &middot; hover the cone, plane or red curve for an explanation.</div>
<!-- @FIGURE_UI_END -->
// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN
/* ── element spec ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// upper nappe        → ConeGeometry(1.8,1.8,64,1,true) flipped, MeshBasic #ccd9f0 op .55 DoubleSide depthWrite false
// lower nappe        → ConeGeometry(1.8,1.8,64,1,true),        same material
// top rim            → LineLoop, circle r=1.8 at y=+1.8, solid #2b4f9e
// bottom rim (near)  → Line, half circle at y=-1.8 facing camera, solid #2b4f9e
// bottom rim (far)   → Line, other half, LineDashedMaterial #2b4f9e
// slant silhouette   → LineSegments apex→rim ×4 (recomputed from camera azimuth), #1f3a6b
// cutting plane      → PlaneGeometry(3.2,3.2) MeshBasic #9aa4b0 op .25 + LineLoop border
// intersection curve → TubeGeometry over analytic samples of plane ∩ cone, MeshBasic #d9453d
// arrowheads         → ConeGeometry(.065,.19) red, at open branch ends along tangent
// flat curve         → TubeGeometry in XY plane: ellipse 1.1×.35 / circle .8 / hyperbola / parabola
// labels             → addLabel: slice title above, conic name below, plane-angle tag
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

const H = 1.8;
const C_FILL = 0xccd9f0, C_LINE = 0x1f3a6b, C_RIM = 0x2b4f9e, C_RED = 0xd9453d, C_PLANE = 0x9aa4b0;

const coneGroup  = new THREE.Group();
const planeGroup = new THREE.Group();
const curveGroup = new THREE.Group();
const flatGroup  = new THREE.Group();
scene.add(coneGroup, planeGroup, curveGroup, flatGroup);

/* ── materials (fade-aware) ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
const matCone      = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: C_FILL, transparent: true, opacity: 0.55, side: THREE.DoubleSide, depthWrite: false });
const matRim       = new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({ color: C_RIM, transparent: true });
const matDash      = new THREE.LineDashedMaterial({ color: C_RIM, transparent: true, dashSize: 0.13, gapSize: 0.09 });
const matEdge      = new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({ color: C_LINE, transparent: true });
const matPlane     = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: C_PLANE, transparent: true, opacity: 0.25, side: THREE.DoubleSide, depthWrite: false });
const matPlaneEdge = new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({ color: 0x6b7684, transparent: true, opacity: 0.65 });
const matRed       = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: C_RED, transparent: true });
const matRedFlat   = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: C_RED, transparent: true });

const GROUP_A = [[matCone, 0.55], [matRim, 1], [matDash, 1], [matEdge, 1], [matPlane, 0.25], [matPlaneEdge, 0.65], [matRed, 1]];
const GROUP_B = [[matRedFlat, 1]];

/* ── cone nappes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
const upGeo = new THREE.ConeGeometry(H, H, 64, 1, true);
upGeo.rotateX(Math.PI); upGeo.translate(0, H / 2, 0);
const upperNappe = new THREE.Mesh(upGeo, matCone);
const loGeo = new THREE.ConeGeometry(H, H, 64, 1, true);
loGeo.translate(0, -H / 2, 0);
const lowerNappe = new THREE.Mesh(loGeo, matCone);
upperNappe.renderOrder = 0; lowerNappe.renderOrder = 0;
coneGroup.add(upperNappe, lowerNappe);

function circlePts(y, n, a0, a1) {
  const p = [];
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
    const a = a0 + (a1 - a0) * i / n;
    p.push(new THREE.Vector3(H * Math.cos(a), y, H * Math.sin(a)));
  }
  return p;
}
const rimTop = new THREE.LineLoop(new THREE.BufferGeometry().setFromPoints(circlePts(H, 64, 0, Math.PI * 2 * 63 / 64)), matRim);
const rimNear = new THREE.Line(new THREE.BufferGeometry(), matRim);
const rimFar  = new THREE.Line(new THREE.BufferGeometry(), matDash);
const silh    = new THREE.LineSegments(new THREE.BufferGeometry(), matEdge);
coneGroup.add(rimTop, rimNear, rimFar, silh);

let _lastAng = 999;
function updateViewDependent() {
  const dir = camera.position.clone().sub(controls.target);
  const ang = Math.atan2(dir.z, dir.x);
  if (Math.abs(ang - _lastAng) < 0.01) return;
  _lastAng = ang;
  rimNear.geometry.dispose();
  rimNear.geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry().setFromPoints(circlePts(-H, 40, ang - Math.PI / 2, ang + Math.PI / 2));
  rimFar.geometry.dispose();
  rimFar.geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry().setFromPoints(circlePts(-H, 40, ang + Math.PI / 2, ang + 3 * Math.PI / 2));
  rimFar.computeLineDistances();
  const arr = [];
  for (const ph of [ang + Math.PI / 2, ang - Math.PI / 2]) {
    const x = H * Math.cos(ph), z = H * Math.sin(ph);
    arr.push(0, 0, 0, x, H, z);
    arr.push(0, 0, 0, x, -H, z);
  }
  silh.geometry.dispose();
  const g = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
  g.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(arr, 3));
  silh.geometry = g;
}

/* ── cutting plane ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
const PS = 3.2;
const planeMesh = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(PS, PS), matPlane);
planeMesh.renderOrder = 1;
const planeEdge = new THREE.LineLoop(new THREE.BufferGeometry().setFromPoints([
  new THREE.Vector3(-PS / 2, -PS / 2, 0), new THREE.Vector3(PS / 2, -PS / 2, 0),
  new THREE.Vector3(PS / 2, PS / 2, 0), new THREE.Vector3(-PS / 2, PS / 2, 0)]), matPlaneEdge);
planeMesh.add(planeEdge);
planeGroup.add(planeMesh);

/* ── analytic intersection ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
function planeParams(deg) {
  const th = THREE.MathUtils.degToRad(deg);
  const t = Math.tan(th);
  let x0 = 0, y0 = 0.9;
  if (deg >= 45) { x0 = 0.5; y0 = 0; }
  else { y0 = Math.min(0.9, Math.max(0.05, 1.5 * (1 - t))); }
  return { th, s: Math.sin(th), c: Math.cos(th), x0, y0 };
}

function extractRuns(pts, valid, wrap) {
  if (valid.every(v => v)) return [{ pts, closed: wrap }];
  const runs = []; let cur = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {
    if (valid[i]) cur.push(pts[i]);
    else { if (cur.length > 1) runs.push({ pts: cur, closed: false }); cur = []; }
  }
  if (cur.length > 1) runs.push({ pts: cur, closed: false });
  if (wrap && runs.length > 1 && valid[0] && valid[pts.length - 1]) {
    const first = runs.shift(), last = runs.pop();
    runs.push({ pts: last.pts.concat(first.pts), closed: false });
  }
  return runs;
}

function buildCurveBranches(deg) {
  const { s, c, x0, y0 } = planeParams(deg);
  const A = s * s - c * c, B = 2 * (y0 * s - x0 * c), C = y0 * y0 - x0 * x0;
  const pt = (a, b) => new THREE.Vector3(x0 + a * c, y0 + a * s, b);
  const out = [];
  if (Math.abs(A) < 1e-4) {                                  // parabola
    let bm = 0;
    for (const sg of [1, -1]) {
      const v = C + B * ((sg * H - y0) / s);
      if (v > bm) bm = v;
    }
    bm = Math.sqrt(Math.max(bm, 1e-4));
    const p = [];
    for (let i = 0; i <= 200; i++) {
      const b = -bm + 2 * bm * i / 200;
      p.push(pt((b * b - C) / B, b));
    }
    out.push({ pts: p, closed: false, open: true });
  } else if (A < 0) {                                        // ellipse / circle
    const ac = -B / (2 * A), val = C - B * B / (4 * A);
    if (val > 0) {
      const bmax = Math.sqrt(val), ah = Math.sqrt(val / -A);
      const N = 280, p = [], ok = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const ph = 2 * Math.PI * i / N;
        const P = pt(ac + ah * Math.cos(ph), bmax * Math.sin(ph));
        p.push(P); ok.push(Math.abs(P.y) <= H + 1e-6);
      }
      for (const r of extractRuns(p, ok, true)) out.push({ pts: r.pts, closed: r.closed, open: !r.closed });
    }
  } else {                                                   // hyperbola
    const ash = -B / (2 * A), D = C - B * B / (4 * A);
    const alpha = Math.sqrt(Math.max(-D, 1e-9) / A), beta = Math.sqrt(Math.max(-D, 1e-9));
    const lim1 = (H - y0) / s, lim2 = (-H - y0) / s;
    const amin = Math.min(lim1, lim2), amax = Math.max(lim1, lim2);
    for (const sg of [1, -1]) {
      const hi = sg > 0 ? (amax - ash) / alpha : (ash - amin) / alpha;
      if (!(hi > 1)) continue;
      const wm = Math.acosh(hi);
      const p = [], ok = [];
      for (let i = 0; i <= 160; i++) {
        const w = -wm + 2 * wm * i / 160;
        const P = pt(sg * alpha * Math.cosh(w) + ash, beta * Math.sinh(w));
        p.push(P); ok.push(Math.abs(P.y) <= H + 1e-6);
      }
      for (const r of extractRuns(p, ok, false)) out.push({ pts: r.pts, closed: false, open: true });
    }
  }
  return out;
}

function clearGroup(g) {
  while (g.children.length) {
    const o = g.children.pop();
    o.geometry?.dispose?.();
    g.remove(o);
  }
}
function addTube(group, pts, closed, mat) {
  if (pts.length < 2) return;
  const crv = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3(pts, closed);
  const seg = Math.min(360, Math.max(16, pts.length));
  const m = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.TubeGeometry(crv, seg, 0.023, 8, closed), mat);
  m.renderOrder = 3;
  group.add(m);
}
function addArrow(group, tip, dir, mat) {
  const g = new THREE.ConeGeometry(0.068, 0.2, 12);
  const m = new THREE.Mesh(g, mat);
  m.quaternion.setFromUnitVectors(new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0), dir.clone().normalize());
  m.position.copy(tip);
  m.renderOrder = 3;
  group.add(m);
}

function kindOf(t) {
  if (t < 0.5) return 'circle';
  if (Math.abs(t - 45) < 0.6) return 'parabola';
  if (t > 45) return 'hyperbola';
  return 'ellipse';
}
const TITLES = { ellipse: 'Diagonal Slice', circle: 'Horizontal Slice', hyperbola: 'Deep Vertical Slice', parabola: 'Vertical Slice' };
const NAMES  = { ellipse: 'Ellipse', circle: 'Circle', hyperbola: 'Hyperbola', parabola: 'Parabola' };

function rebuildCurve(deg) {
  clearGroup(curveGroup);
  const k = kindOf(deg);
  const branches = buildCurveBranches(deg);
  for (const br of branches) {
    addTube(curveGroup, br.pts, br.closed, matRed);
    if (br.open && (k === 'parabola' || k === 'hyperbola') && br.pts.length > 3) {
      const n = br.pts.length;
      addArrow(curveGroup, br.pts[n - 1], br.pts[n - 1].clone().sub(br.pts[n - 2]), matRed);
      addArrow(curveGroup, br.pts[0], br.pts[0].clone().sub(br.pts[1]), matRed);
    }
  }
}

/* ── flat (isolated) curve ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
function rebuildFlat(k) {
  clearGroup(flatGroup);
  if (k === 'ellipse' || k === 'circle') {
    const rx = k === 'circle' ? 0.8 : 1.1, ry = k === 'circle' ? 0.8 : 0.35;
    const p = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < 120; i++) {
      const a = 2 * Math.PI * i / 120;
      p.push(new THREE.Vector3(rx * Math.cos(a), ry * Math.sin(a), 0));
    }
    addTube(flatGroup, p, true, matRedFlat);
  } else if (k === 'hyperbola') {
    for (const sg of [1, -1]) {
      const p = [];
      for (let i = 0; i <= 90; i++) {
        const x = -1.1 + 2.2 * i / 90;
        p.push(new THREE.Vector3(x, sg * 0.35 * Math.sqrt(1 + x * x / 0.25), 0));
      }
      addTube(flatGroup, p, false, matRedFlat);
    }
  } else {
    const p = [];
    for (let i = 0; i <= 90; i++) {
      const x = -1.1 + 2.2 * i / 90;
      p.push(new THREE.Vector3(x, 0.7 * x * x - 0.5, 0));
    }
    addTube(flatGroup, p, false, matRedFlat);
    const n = p.length;
    addArrow(flatGroup, p[n - 1], p[n - 1].clone().sub(p[n - 2]), matRedFlat);
    addArrow(flatGroup, p[0], p[0].clone().sub(p[1]), matRedFlat);
  }
}

function placePlane(deg) {
  const { th, x0, y0 } = planeParams(deg);
  planeMesh.position.set(x0, y0, 0);
  planeMesh.quaternion.setFromEuler(new THREE.Euler(-Math.PI / 2, 0, 0));
  planeMesh.quaternion.premultiply(new THREE.Quaternion().setFromAxisAngle(new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, 1), th));
}

/* ── initial build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
const figState = { tilt: 25, mode: 'cone', showPlane: true };
rebuildCurve(figState.tilt);
rebuildFlat(kindOf(figState.tilt));
placePlane(figState.tilt);
updateViewDependent();

/* ── camera ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
function applyCamera(mode) {
  const others = mode === 'flat' ? [coneGroup, planeGroup, curveGroup] : [flatGroup];
  others.forEach(g => scene.remove(g));
  if (mode === 'flat') setCameraView({ projection: 'orthographic', axisScreenAngles: null, rollDeg: 0, heightFraction: 0.6 });
  else setCameraView({ projection: 'orthographic', axisScreenAngles: { x: 30, z: 30 }, rollDeg: 0, heightFraction: 0.7 });
  others.forEach(g => scene.add(g));
}
applyCamera('cone');

/* ── labels ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
const labelTitle = addLabel(TITLES.ellipse, new THREE.Vector3(0, H + 0.62, 0), { bold: true, fontSize: '15px', color: '#1a1a1a' });
const labelName  = addLabel(NAMES.ellipse, new THREE.Vector3(0, -H - 0.78, 0), { bold: true, fontSize: '14px', color: '#1a1a1a' });
const labelAngle = addLabel('&theta; = 25&deg;', new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, 0), { fontSize: '11px', color: '#5a6672' });

function updateLabels() {
  const k = kindOf(figState.tilt);
  labelTitle.div.innerHTML = TITLES[k];
  labelName.div.innerHTML = NAMES[k];
  if (figState.mode === 'cone') {
    labelTitle.pos.set(0, H + 0.62, 0);
    labelName.pos.set(0, -H - 0.8, 0);
    const { s, c, x0, y0 } = planeParams(figState.tilt);
    labelAngle.pos.set(x0 - 1.72 * c, y0 - 1.72 * s, 0);
    labelAngle.div.innerHTML = 'plane &theta; = ' + Math.round(figState.tilt) + '&deg;';
  } else {
    labelTitle.pos.set(0, 1.45, 0);
    labelName.pos.set(0, -1.22, 0);
  }
}
updateLabels();

/* ── interactivity (hover / click) ──────────────────────────────────────── */
registerInteractive(upperNappe, {
  title: 'Upper nappe',
  tooltip: 'Upper nappe of the double cone',
  body: 'A right circular cone of slant 45°: every point satisfies y² = x² + z². The double cone is two such nappes meeting apex to apex at the origin.'
});
registerInteractive(lowerNappe, {
  title: 'Lower nappe',
  tooltip: 'Lower nappe of the double cone',
  body: 'Only a plane steeper than the 45° slant can reach both nappes — that is exactly when the intersection splits into the two branches of a hyperbola.'
});
registerInteractive(planeMesh, {
  title: 'Cutting plane',
  tooltip: 'The generating plane — drag the tilt slider',
  body: 'The plane pivots about the world Z axis. Its tilt θ measured from horizontal, compared with the cone’s 45° slant, decides the conic: θ=0 circle, 0<θ<45 ellipse, θ=45 parabola, θ>45 hyperbola.'
});
registerInteractive(curveGroup, {
  title: 'Intersection curve',
  tooltip: 'Plane ∩ cone — the conic section',
  body: 'Substituting the plane’s parameterisation into y² = x² + z² gives a quadratic in the plane’s own coordinates — the conic. Switch to “Curve alone” to see it flattened.'
});

/* ── fading between modes ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
let modeT = 0, modeTarget = 0, camMode = 'cone';
function applyFade() {
  const a = 1 - modeT, b = modeT;
  for (const [m, base] of GROUP_A) m.opacity = base * a;
  for (const [m, base] of GROUP_B) m.opacity = base * b;
  coneGroup.visible = a > 0.01;
  curveGroup.visible = a > 0.01;
  planeGroup.visible = a > 0.01 && figState.showPlane;
  flatGroup.visible = b > 0.01;
  labelAngle.div.style.opacity = (a > 0.5 && figState.showPlane) ? '1' : '0';
}
applyFade();

/* ── UI wiring ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
document.getElementById('btnReset').style.display = '';
const slider = document.getElementById('planeTilt');
const tiltVal = document.getElementById('tiltVal');
const kbtns = {
  ellipse: document.getElementById('btnKEllipse'),
  circle: document.getElementById('btnKCircle'),
  hyperbola: document.getElementById('btnKHyper'),
  parabola: document.getElementById('btnKPara')
};
const bCone = document.getElementById('btnViewCone');
const bFlat = document.getElementById('btnViewFlat');

let lastKind = kindOf(figState.tilt);
function refresh(rebuildAll = true) {
  const k = kindOf(figState.tilt);
  if (rebuildAll) { rebuildCurve(figState.tilt); placePlane(figState.tilt); }
  if (k !== lastKind) { rebuildFlat(k); lastKind = k; flashLabels(); }
  slider.value = String(Math.round(figState.tilt));
  tiltVal.innerHTML = Math.round(figState.tilt) + '&deg;';
  for (const key in kbtns) kbtns[key].classList.toggle('active', key === k);
  bCone.classList.toggle('active', figState.mode === 'cone');
  bFlat.classList.toggle('active', figState.mode === 'flat');
  updateLabels();
  applyFade();
}

let flashUntil = 0;
function flashLabels() { flashUntil = performance.now() + 700; }

function setMode(m) {
  if (figState.mode === m) return;
  figState.mode = m;
  modeTarget = m === 'flat' ? 1 : 0;
  refresh(false);
}

slider.addEventListener('input', () => {
  stopPlay();
  tiltTween = null;
  figState.tilt = parseFloat(slider.value);
  refresh();
});
for (const key in kbtns) {
  kbtns[key].addEventListener('click', () => {
    stopPlay();
    setMode('cone');
    tweenTilt({ ellipse: 25, circle: 0, hyperbola: 70, parabola: 45 }[key]);
    flashLabels();
  });
}
bCone.addEventListener('click', () => { stopPlay(); setMode('cone'); });
bFlat.addEventListener('click', () => { stopPlay(); setMode('flat'); });
document.getElementById('chkPlane').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
  figState.showPlane = e.target.checked;
  applyFade();
});

/* ── tilt tween + demo steps ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
let tiltTween = null;
function tweenTilt(to, dur = 700) {
  tiltTween = { from: figState.tilt, to, t: 0, dur };
}

const STEPS = [
  { title: 'Diagonal Slice → Ellipse', n: 'A plane tilted about 25° cuts clean through the upper nappe, and the closed red curve is a stretched oval: an ellipse.', tilt: 25, mode: 'cone' },
  { title: 'Flatten it', n: 'Lift the ellipse out of the cone and view it face-on — the same red curve is the planar graph labeled Ellipse.', tilt: 25, mode: 'flat' },
  { title: 'Horizontal Slice → Circle', n: 'Level the plane to 0°. The cut is perpendicular to the axis and the ellipse closes up into a perfect circle.', tilt: 0, mode: 'cone' },
  { title: 'Vertical Slice → Parabola', n: 'Tilt the plane until it is exactly parallel to the cone’s slant edge (45°). The curve can no longer close: it runs off as a single parabolic arc through the lower nappe.', tilt: 45, mode: 'cone' },
  { title: 'Deep Vertical Slice → Hyperbola', n: 'Past 45° the plane is steep enough to reach both nappes at once, so the intersection splits into two opposing red branches — a hyperbola.', tilt: 70, mode: 'cone' },
  { title: 'Compare the four graphs', n: 'Switch to the isolated curves and step back through the sequence: oval, circle, two branches, single arc — the full set of nondegenerate conic sections.', tilt: 70, mode: 'flat' }
];
let stepIdx = 0;
const stepTitle = document.getElementById('stepTitle');
const narration = document.getElementById('narration');

function goToStep(i) {
  stepIdx = (i + STEPS.length) % STEPS.length;
  const st = STEPS[stepIdx];
  stepTitle.textContent = (stepIdx + 1) + '/' + STEPS.length + '  ' + st.title;
  narration.textContent = st.n;
  setMode(st.mode);
  tweenTilt(st.tilt);
  flashLabels();
}
goToStep(0);

let playTimer = null;
function stopPlay() {
  if (playTimer) { clearInterval(playTimer); playTimer = null; document.getElementById('btnPlay').textContent = '▶ Play'; }
}
document.getElementById('btnPrev').addEventListener('click', () => { stopPlay(); goToStep(stepIdx - 1); });
document.getElementById('btnNext').addEventListener('click', () => { stopPlay(); goToStep(stepIdx + 1); });
document.getElementById('btnPlay').addEventListener('click', () => {
  if (playTimer) { stopPlay(); return; }
  document.getElementById('btnPlay').textContent = '❚❚ Pause';
  goToStep(stepIdx + 1);
  playTimer = setInterval(() => goToStep(stepIdx + 1), 3600);
});

/* ── own animation loop for tweens / view-dependent lines ───────────────── */
let _prevT = performance.now();
function figTick() {
  requestAnimationFrame(figTick);
  const now = performance.now();
  const dt = Math.min(0.05, (now - _prevT) / 1000);
  _prevT = now;

  if (tiltTween) {
    tiltTween.t += dt * 1000;
    const u = Math.min(1, tiltTween.t / tiltTween.dur);
    const e = u < 0.5 ? 2 * u * u : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * u + 2, 2) / 2;
    figState.tilt = tiltTween.from + (tiltTween.to - tiltTween.from) * e;
    if (u >= 1) { figState.tilt = tiltTween.to; tiltTween = null; }
    refresh();
  }

  if (Math.abs(modeT - modeTarget) > 0.001) {
    modeT += (modeTarget - modeT) * Math.min(1, dt / 0.3 * 2.2);
    if (Math.abs(modeT - modeTarget) <= 0.001) modeT = modeTarget;
    applyFade();
    const want = modeT > 0.5 ? 'flat' : 'cone';
    if (want !== camMode) { camMode = want; applyCamera(want); updateLabels(); }
  }

  const flashing = now < flashUntil;
  const col = flashing ? '#d9453d' : '#1a1a1a';
  labelTitle.div.style.color = col;
  labelName.div.style.color = col;

  if (camMode === 'cone') updateViewDependent();
}
